sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (Nick 2026-11-07): stage 6 of the command development pipeline. When a release changed playbooks, pins or lock files, and once a day, every task VM host bakes its next image from its current one: one VM, one Ansible run that converges everything, then the image and its seed are published. Idle slots then re-enrol from it with their fixed identities. Nothing is copied between hosts. The per-host run: docs/cli/tasks/vm-image-refresh.mmd.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: development pipeline stage 6 · per-host task image and seed refresh
  %% kind: pipeline.6-task-image-seed-refresh
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=each host tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=refresh VM tone=gray
  %% lane SL icon=server pill=slots tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>one run per host
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Refresh VM<br/>current image
  participant SL as Slots<br/>fixed identities
  Note over GW: Start the refresh<br/>release · daily
  %%> Triggers:
  %%> - a release whose commit changed what the image carries: the playbooks (`swamp/ansible`), the pins (`apps/gateway/resources/machine-software`) and the lock files (`TaskVmImageInputs`); a code-only release needs none, because a slot fetches its task branch
  %%> - a daily Schedule; it only dispatches the admission
  %%> - a host with a refresh open returns it
  GW->>SW: Start one run per host<br/>all in parallel
  %%> Why:
  %%> - each host bakes its own image and seed; copying them between hosts is not a supported flow
  loop each task VM host, in parallel
    SW->>H: Start the refresh VM<br/>from the current image
    SW->>VM: Converge everything<br/>one Ansible run
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - outer VM: packages, tools, Swamp, orbit-agent, the Pi server, sshd and UFW at the release's pins
    %%> - the warm checkout: main at the release commit, with `vendor/` and `node_modules/`
    %%> - each container: its role phases, the checkout device, migrations, services running; then a new `base` snapshot of each
    SW->>H: Publish the image<br/>image and seed
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - stops the refresh VM, publishes it as the candidate image and its container disk as the candidate's seed; the refresh VM is deleted
    SW->>SL: Re-enrol one slot<br/>proves the candidate
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - rebuilds the first idle slot from the candidate with its fixed identity, takes its `clean` snapshot and runs the claim's ready check; it proves exactly what a claim gets
    SW->>H: Promote<br/>keep -previous
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - the alias moves to the candidate, the old image keeps `-previous` for rollback, and older images are removed
    SW->>SL: Re-enrol idle slots<br/>one at a time
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - each other idle slot re-enrols from the new image; a claimed slot re-enrols when it is released
    opt a new host or a new base OS
      SW->>H: Build from the recipe<br/>once, not per release
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - builds the first image from the stock image (`task_vm.image_build`); every later release only refreshes it
    end
  end
  alt every host refreshed
    SW-->>GW: Host refreshed<br/>terminal event per host
    Note over GW: Record the new image<br/>claims use it
    %%> Result:
    %%> - target about 3 min per host; one slow host does not hold the others
  else a refresh failed
    SW--xGW: Host not refreshed<br/>failed step
    Note over GW: Alert · try again<br/>next trigger
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the host keeps its image; the refresh VM and the candidate are removed, and the proving slot re-enrols from the current image
  end
